Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:55:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 195/209] feat(area): distributor function component

The component form of CSplineDistributor, and the case that motivated the whole
spline family: "the distributor could do far more as a function component on a
spline than locked inside one object". Category "Area", label "Distributor".

OWNERSHIP is the load-bearing part (decision 04, D1). The instances are render
nodes this component owns, created as eERType_MovableBrush with
SetOwnerEntity(m_pEntity) - the same two calls an entity slot makes for a static
mesh (EntitySlot.cpp:135-145). Both halves matter, and both come out of
research/08 section 2.7: COctreeNode::SaveObjects skips every node with an owner
entity (ObjectsTree_Serialize.cpp:295, :321), and plain eERType_Brush is the
serialized brush type (:398) while eERType_MovableBrush is not in the list at
all, so the export skips these nodes even if an owner is ever lost.
SetOwnerEntity is also only implemented on CMovableBrush (Brush.h:142-152); on a
plain CBrush it asserts. The level therefore stores the parameters and the seed,
not thousands of brushes.

FEATURE SET, against legacy's one mesh / one step / follow on-off / one Z angle:
a weighted mesh list, a stored Seed, three spacing modes (Fixed Step, Fixed
Count, Density) with spacing jitter, four alignment modes (Follow Tangent, World
Up, Surface Normal, Fixed), a scale range plus a linear ramp along the curve plus
an optional multiply by the spline's own per-point width, per-axis rotation
jitter, an offset range in the instance's own frame, start and end trim, skip
probability, an end-cap mesh at each end of an open curve, snap to terrain, and
the full legacy brush render-flag block with view-distance and LOD ratios.

DETERMINISM: a private xorshift32 stream seeded from Seed mixed with the
instance index, drawn in a fixed order (skip, mesh, spacing, scale, rotation,
offset) so that turning one feature off does not reshuffle everything after it.
cry_random is deliberately not used - it is seeded globally, so the same level
would place differently on every run.

COST WHEN IDLE IS ZERO: no update event. Rebuilds happen on a shape change
(already one per edit gesture, because the shape coalesces BeginEdit/EndEdit),
on a property change, and transform-only on a move - the fast path
CSplineDistributor::InvalidateTM takes (:204-212), here with the instance list
reused so that a move cannot reshuffle which mesh went where.

"Bake To Brushes" is a no-op that warns, as planned (D4). Baking means creating
editor objects - one CBrushObject per instance inside one undo step - and an
engine module cannot reach the object manager; the seam belongs in
AreaComponentsEditor, driven from a tool, like "Edit Shape" already is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
